module

public import CFSG.Quasithin.MainConverse.AlternatingSections.NineReduction.Primitive.SimpleRecognition.TripleRigidity.Exclude1512.Generators

/-!
# Explicit enumeration data for the first nine-point seed

Rows are breadth-first words in the published `cycle` and `involution false`.
Each permutation is packed in base nine, with its image of 0 as the units digit.
The parent column records a shorter word. The two successor and predecessor
columns record right multiplication by the generators and their inverses.
The last table recovers a row number from the images of 0, 1 and 2.

These are witness data only. The companion module checks every permutation,
transition, parent edge and row discriminator by kernel reduction before using
subgroup closure induction to prove the exact order.

Source context: Aschbacher–Smith, `refs/quasithin.pdf`, printed pp.4 and 482,
condition K and the alternating case. The data are computed directly from the
permutations in `Exclude1512.Generators`, without model recognition.
-/

@[expose] public section
namespace CFSG.Quasithin.MainConverse.NineReduction.Exclude1512.SeedEnumeration

